      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor of Business Analytics and Sports Management",
      "description": "Assistant/Associate Professor of Business Analytics and Sports Management Salary Depends on Qualifications Location Alma Job Type Faculty - Full-Time Tenure Track Job Number 2026-00037 Division Social Sciences Department Business Administration Opening Date 08/26/2026 Closing Date 10/29/2026 11:59 PM Eastern FLSA Exempt Description Benefits POSITION SUMMARY The Department of Business Administration at Alma College invites applications for a full-time, tenure-track Assistant/Associate Professor of Business Analytics and Sports Management beginning August 2027. The standard teaching load is six units throughout the academic year. Teaching experience and/or professional experience in sports management, general business, and business analytics (Excel, descriptive statistics, and visual tools such as Power BI) are required. The department desires an experienced faculty colleague with a demonstrated commitment to excellence in undergraduate teaching and significant analytics capability. The successful candidate will be able to teach sports management courses and business analytics courses at various levels and have excellent attention to detail. Class sizes at Alma College are small, and experiential learning is utilized. REQUIRED QUALIFICATIONS - A Ph.D. or a Doctor of Business Administration (DBA) in a related business field is required. An all-but-dissertation (ABD) with the degree completed before the start date will be considered for the position - Experience teaching advanced Excel, descriptive statistics, MS Power BI, or similar applications - Evidence of (or strong potential for) excellence in undergraduate teaching. PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS - Experience in the sports management industry - Experience with Canvas or other LMS - An ability to teach other business courses as required. - Hands-on proficiency with modern AI/ML tools and methods relevant to business, such as R, Python, and LLMs, is a plus. Alma College is classified as a selective Baccalaureate College: Diverse Fields by the Carnegie Foundation for the Advancement of Teaching. Alma is committed to academic excellence and the development of responsible leaders; our students thrive on challenging academic programs in a supportive, small-college environment emphasizing active, collaborative learning and close student-faculty interaction. Alma is a private Phi Beta Kappa institution located in the center of Michigan’s Lower Peninsula. Alma College is an Equal Opportunity Employer and is committed to recruiting and retaining a diverse faculty, staff, and student body. Alma College recognizes that we are all transformed when we celebrate and value the varied identities, backgrounds, experiences, and perspectives in our campus community. We are committed to recognizing and removing barriers to success and providing equitable access to opportunities through education and advocacy. In our increasingly diverse campus and world, we pledge to create a climate where everyone is safe and free to grow intellectually, spiritually, and emotionally. We offer a comprehensive benefits package to employees in eligible positions working 30 hours or more per week. Benefits include medical, dental, and vision coverage; retirement plans; flexible spending accounts; life insurance; long-term disability; paid holidays; vacation; and sick leave. Part-time employees who average 20 hours per week over the course of a year are eligible for select benefits on a prorated basis. For additional details, please visit our Prospective Employees page. Employer Alma College (MI) Address 614 W. Superior St. Alma, Michigan, 48801 Phone 989-463-7467 Website https://www.alma.edu Apply"
