      "title": "Lecturer of Business Administration",
      "description": "Lecturer of Business Administration Salary Depends on Qualifications Location Alma Job Type Faculty - Full-Time Non-Tenure Track Job Number 2026-00048 Division Social Sciences Department Business Administration Opening Date 10/15/2026 Closing Date Continuous FLSA Exempt Description Benefits POSITION SUMMARY The Alma College Department of Business Administration invites applications for the position of Lecturer in Business Administration with a specialty in Business Law and Management. This is a full-time, non-tenure track position beginning August 2027. The term is three years with the possibility of renewal. The standard teaching load is eight units throughout the academic year. Review of applicants will begin on January 11, 2027, and continue until the position is filled. ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS The department desires an experienced faculty colleague with a demonstrated commitment to excellence in undergraduate teaching and excellent attention to detail. We are seeking a business law instructor who can also teach management and other business courses. Experience teaching business analytics and AI would be beneficial and preferred. Class sizes at Alma College are small, and experiential learning is utilized. REQUIRED QUALIFICATIONS - Juris Doctor (J.D.) - Teaching and/or professional experience in business law and management - Commitment to excellence in undergraduate teaching in a liberal arts setting PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS - Current or past experience as a practicing attorney in a business environment - Ph.D. or DBA in business, or an MBA in addition to a J.D. - Experience teaching management, leadership, and other business courses - Experience with teaching analytics courses and/or AI - Experience with Canvas or other LMS Alma College is classified as a selective Baccalaureate College: Diverse Fields by the Carnegie Foundation for the Advancement of Teaching. Alma is committed to academic excellence and the development of responsible leaders;